    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:196`). I've split it into the framework-level gates that run before the method body and then each step inside the method, tagging each as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state), noting that several are both.\n\n## Before the method body (framework)\n\n1. **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[validation] Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (declared on the generated `OwnersApi`). Constraints on the DTO:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `title`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `email` \u2014 `@Size` bounds when present\n   - (Jackson deserialization also applies; `OwnerJacksonConfig` only affects *responses* \u2014 it hides the write-only `sharesHousehold` on the way out.)\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n3. **Read idempotency key** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header, trimmed; blank \u21d2 treated as absent.\n4. **[side-effect / short-circuit] Idempotency replay** \u2014 if the key was seen before, looks up the previously created owner and returns it with **200 OK**, skipping everything below.\n5. **[side-effect] Address resolution** (`addressResolver.resolve`) \u2014 mutates the DTO in place: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address`, then sets the flat `address` to the composed structured address (line1 + space + line2) when `addressLine1` is present, otherwise the normalized flat address.\n6. **[validation] Required-fields check** (`ownerFieldsValidator.findMissingOrBlankFields`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, an address (either `addressLine1` or `address`), `city`, `telephone` must be present and non-blank; otherwise throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n7. **[side-effect] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 id/pets/householdId ignored.\n8. **[side-effect] Namesake count** \u2014 looks up active (non-deleted) owners with the same last name (case-insensitive) and sets `namesakeCount`.\n9. **[side-effect] Household assignment** (`assignHousehold`) \u2014 sets `householdId` (deterministically derived from last name + postcode), finds existing household members, and sets `householdSize` (members + 1).\n10. **[side-effect + validation] Telephone normalization** (`telephoneNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 `setTelephone`) \u2014 converts to E.164; throws `InvalidTelephoneException` if it can't form a valid number (8\u201315 digits, correct national length for known country codes).\n11. **[side-effect + validation] Email normalization** (`emailNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 `setEmail`) \u2014 lower-cases; throws `InvalidEmailException` if present but syntactically invalid (null allowed).\n12. **[validation] Disposable email domain** (`disposableEmailDomainValidator.validate`) \u2014 throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` if the domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n13. **[validation] Postcode** (`postcodeValidator.validate`) \u2014 if present, must be exactly 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4 digits); otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n14. **[validation] Hard duplicate identity** (`rejectIfDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 among active owners with the same (normalized) telephone, throws `DuplicateIdentityException` if the full identity key already exists.\n15. **[validation + side-effect] Household rule** (`applyHouseholdRule`):\n    - New household \u21d2 **[side-effect]** run possible-duplicate detection, setting `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n    - Joins an existing household without `sharesHousehold=true` \u21d2 throws `HouseholdDuplicateException`.\n    - Declared member (`sharesHousehold=true`) \u21d2 **[side-effect]** clears `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.\n16. **[validation] Registration date** (`registrationDateValidator.validate`) \u2014 if present, must not be after today; otherwise `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n17. **[side-effect] Default registration date** \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n18. **[side-effect] Business-day adjustment** \u2014 `setRegistrationDate(BusinessDayResolver.toBusinessDay(...))`.\n19. **[validation] Daily owner limit** \u2014 counts owners already registered on that (adjusted) date; if `>= DailyOwnerLimitException.MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n20. **[side-effect] Bulk-signup warning** \u2014 `setBulkSignupWarning(...)` based on the day's count.\n21. **[validation] City owner limit** \u2014 counts owners in the city; if `>= CityOwnerLimitException.MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`, throws `CityOwnerLimitException`.\n22. **[side-effect] Customer code** (`assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `setCustomerCode`) \u2014 generates a code from region/telephone/last name and de-duplicates against existing codes with the same prefix.\n23. **[side-effect] Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`) \u2014 saves the owner (assigns its id).\n24. **[side-effect] Record idempotency key** \u2014 if a key was supplied, `idempotencyStore.record(key, owner.getId())`.\n25. **[side-effect] Audit log** (`ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated`).\n26. **[side-effect] Build response** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived output fields (displayName, initials, salutation, telephoneDisplay, customerCode check digit, membershipNumber/points/level, fiscalYear, locality, timezone, contactPreference, identityKey, ageBand, selfLink), sets the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, and returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n### Two things worth flagging\n- **`addOwner` is not `@Transactional`** (unlike `deleteOwner`). The count-then-check limits in steps 19 and 21, the identity/household duplicate checks, and the customer-code dedup all read-then-write without a surrounding transaction, so they're subject to races under concurrent creates.\n- Steps 8\u201315 mutate the mapped `Owner` **before** the limit checks (19, 21) and before persistence, but since nothing is saved until step 23, a rejection at any later validation simply aborts with no persisted state (only the in-memory `Owner`/DTO were mutated)."
